\subsection{Selecting times}%
\label{medvind.select}

The attest view returns the times of everyone in the plan, for every
work leader---hundreds of rows for a department.
We select among them on four properties, all optional and combined
with \enquote{and}:
\begin{description}
\item[The TA] by name or by personnummer, see below.
\item[The work leader] a regular expression matched against
  [[arbledare_orsak]], so that a teacher finds the times reported to
  them.
\item[The comment] a regular expression matched against
  [[tidtyp_orsak]]; TAs tend to put the course code there, as in
  \enquote{DD1301 labbpass}.
\item[Attested or not] a time is attested once its [[atteststatus]] is
  [[A]]. The ones that are not are the ones that still need checking.
\end{description}
The regular expressions are searched for, not matched in full, and
case is ignored, so \enquote{dd1301} finds \enquote{DD1301 labbpass}.

<<functions>>=
def select(records, ta=None, leader=None, comment=None, attested=None):
    """Return the records that satisfy all the given criteria.

    `ta` is a name regex or a personnummer (see `matches_ta`); `leader`
    and `comment` are regexes searched case-insensitively in the work
    leader and the comment; `attested` is True for attested times only,
    False for unattested only and None for both.
    """
    return [
        record
        for record in records
        if (ta is None or matches_ta(record, ta))
        and (leader is None
             or searches(leader, record.get("arbledare_orsak", "")))
        and (comment is None
             or searches(comment, record.get("tidtyp_orsak", "")))
        and (attested is None or is_attested(record) == attested)
    ]

def searches(pattern, text):
    """Return True if the regex `pattern` occurs in `text`, ignoring case."""
    return re.search(pattern, text, re.IGNORECASE) is not None

def is_attested(record):
    """Return True if the time in `record` has been attested."""
    return record.get("atteststatus") == ATTESTED
<<constants>>=
ATTESTED = "A"
<<imports>>=
import re
@

\paragraph{Selecting a TA.}
A name is how the attest view shows a TA, so a name is what a teacher
will type.
But names are ambiguous, and a personnummer is not.
Rather than adding an option for each, we tell them apart by their
form: a personnummer is ten or twelve digits, perhaps with a [[-]] or,
for those over a hundred, a [[+]] before the last four; nobody's name
looks like that.
Medvind writes the personnummer with ten digits, so we compare the
last ten digits of both.
<<constants>>=
PERSONNUMMER = re.compile(r"(\d{2})?(\d{6})[-+]?(\d{4})")
<<functions>>=
def matches_ta(record, pattern):
    """Return True if `record` was reported by the TA `pattern`.

    A `pattern` shaped like a personnummer (10 or 12 digits, optionally
    with `-` or `+`) is compared with the record's personnummer;
    anything else is a regex searched for in the full name.
    """
    personnummer = PERSONNUMMER.fullmatch(pattern.strip())
    if personnummer:
        wanted = personnummer.group(2) + personnummer.group(3)
        return re.sub(r"\D", "", record.get("realpnr", ""))[-10:] == wanted
    return searches(pattern, full_name(record))
